<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">FUNCINPEC</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1981">1981</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">FUNCINPEC is a Cambodian royalist party founded by Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Norodom Sihanouk</a> in 1981 as a resistance movement against the Vietnamese-backed government. Its French acronym stands for National United Front for an Independent, Neutral, Peaceful and Cooperative <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>. Under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-ranariddh">Norodom Ranariddh</a> it won the United Nations-run election of 1993 and shared power with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodian-peoples-party">Cambodian People's Party</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-sen">Hun Sen</a> ousted Ranariddh in 1997, after which it declined.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/funcinpec.jpg" alt="FUNCINPEC" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FUNCINPEC · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FUNCINPEC_logo.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
